@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] export-channel-no-elevation-or-shell
The bridge runs only as the dedicated SSH account with a server-selected key
argv; SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND is validated into a fixed record and remote text is
never executed. The serve side verifies SO_PEERCRED against the dedicated
account, accepts exactly one writable descriptor with the bounded frame, and
exposes only the selected key/request to the fixed worker argv. No setuid or
capabilities on either side; worker stderr and data paths never become helper
diagnostics.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] export-channel-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover the record encode/decode roundtrip, decode totality
over arbitrary bytes (no panic, acceptance only at exactly WIRE_BYTES and only
for canonical encodings), the selector lattice and the charset/bound rules with
an independent spec; process fixtures cover peercred refusal, listener/socket
custody, descriptor forwarding, disconnect cancellation and completion
authentication.
